---
import Card from '../../components/Card.astro';
import MediaBlock from '../../components/MediaBlock.astro';
import CookieBanner from '../../components/react/CookieBanner';
import LogoWheel from '../../components/react/LogoWheel';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Become a member';
const description = 'Join the Xen community and become a member to actively contribute to the advancement of open-source virtualization.';
const keywords = ['Xen Project', 'membership', 'open source', 'community involvement', 'contributors', 'benefits', 'participation', 'collaboration', 'virtualization', 'governance'];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} keywords={keywords}>
  <article class="article page-single">
    <div class="container page-top"><h1>{title}</h1><div class="description">{description}</div></div>
    <div class="single-content">
      <Section>
        <MediaBlock title="The Xen Project members are companies that are committed to the market and technical success of the Xen Project" media="/img/flatline/brainstorming-session.svg" alt="Illustration of three people having a discussion with speech bubbles, symbolizing teamwork and communication." animate>
          <p>The Xen Project members are companies that are committed to the market and technical success of the Xen Project.</p>
          <p>The Members are complementary to the role of committers and maintainers, with both working closely together to ensure the overall priorities of the project are aligned.</p>
          <p>Committers and maintainers are responsible for the technical development and are the final decision makers on code contributions to the Xen Project.</p>
          <p class="mg-t-lg"><a href="https://enrollment.lfx.linuxfoundation.org/?project=xen" class="btn btn-primary">Join now <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></p>
        </MediaBlock>
      </Section>

      <Section class="section-square-rounded">
        <h2 class="txt-c">Main responsibilities</h2>
        <div class="row row-from-list" style="--cols: 2">
          <Card title="Financial oversight" titleLevel={2} class="card--bg-white">Budget management and investment decisions on infrastructure and project operations.</Card>
          <Card title="Annual pricing" titleLevel={2} class="card--bg-white"><p><strong>Premier Member:</strong> $40,000</p><p><strong>Advisory Board Governing Member:</strong> $30,000</p><p><strong>Startup Member*:</strong> $10,000</p><p><strong>Associate Member**:</strong> Free</p><p><em>* Startup members must have less than 100 employees and require approval from Governing Board Members.</em></p><p><em>** Associate Members are free and available to pre-approved Associate Members of The Linux Foundation e.g. Government or Academic institutions</em></p></Card>
          <Card title="Steer the project" titleLevel={2} class="card--bg-white">To advance its market and technical success by raising awareness.</Card>
          <Card title="Global policy decisions" titleLevel={2} class="card--bg-white">Trademarks, compliance requirements, test cases, and infrastructure.</Card>
        </div>
      </Section>

      <Section>
        <MediaBlock title="Improve engineering ROI" media="/img/flatline/data-analysis.svg" alt="Illustration of a person analyzing data, symbolizing data analysis and decision-making." mediaPosition="right" animate>
          <p>The Xen Project is in the process of creating a new common test infrastructure. New test cases for specific hardware and software combinations will lead to higher quality project releases. In addition, a planned focus on a security and hardening framework will enhance the release readiness of the Xen Project.</p>
          <p>The Advisory Board helps define test cases and prioritize release requirements, in cooperation with project maintainers, ultimately increasing engineering ROI from the impact of these decisions.</p>
        </MediaBlock>
      </Section>
      <Section>
        <MediaBlock title="Xen Project Insights" media="/img/flatline/data-analyst.svg" alt="Illustration of a person interacting with charts and graphs on a tablet, representing data visualization and analysis." animate>
          <p>Board members can propose and vote upon changes to the Xen Project test and validation infrastructure and financial resource allocation.</p>
          <p>By being an active Advisory Board participant, regular opportunities for discussions with technical leaders include the chance to share priorities and endorse new strategies. In return, members will gain valuable strategic insight into project plans and future scope.</p>
        </MediaBlock>
      </Section>
      <Section>
        <MediaBlock title="Increase visibility" media="/img/flatline/handshake.svg" alt="Illustration of two people shaking hands, symbolizing partnership and agreement." mediaPosition="right" animate>
          <p>Board members can influence the marketing strategy and participate in a wide range of activities including press releases, brand visibility on the website, and giveaways at events.</p>
        </MediaBlock>
      </Section>
      <Section>
        <MediaBlock title="Define policies" media="/img/flatline/brainstorming.svg" alt="Illustration of a light bulb with a brain inside and speech bubbles around it, symbolizing innovation and creative thinking." animate>
          <p>Members help define policies, including trademark usage, compliance and certification of Xen derivatives. In addition, membership dues funds project infrastructure, such as hosting and test environments which are essential to the project.</p>
          <p>The Board process will help ensure non-technical decisions are collectively determined. As such, the Advisory Board contributes a sustainable, self-directed source of funding for work that will help drive the marketplace and technical success of the Xen Project.</p>
        </MediaBlock>
      </Section>

      <Section class="section-square-primary">
        <h2 class="txt-c">How to <strong>join?</strong></h2>
        <div class="row row-from-list" style="--cols: 3">
          <Card title="Step 1" class="card--bg-white">Review membership benefits and requirements on the Xen Project website.</Card>
          <Card title="Step 2" class="card--bg-white">Contact the Xen Project team to discuss membership options and fees.</Card>
          <Card title="Step 3" class="card--bg-white">Complete the membership application and submit payment to join.</Card>
        </div>
        <p class="txt-c mg-t-lg"><a href="https://enrollment.lfx.linuxfoundation.org/?project=xen" class="btn btn-primary">Join now <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></p>
        <p class="txt-c">Need some help? <a href="mailto:community.manager@xenproject.org"><strong>Email us here</strong></a></p>
      </Section>

      <Section>
        <MediaBlock title="Governed by Xen project members" mediaPosition="right" animate>
          <p>Board members can propose and vote upon changes to the Xen Project. Members also gain valuable strategic insight into project plans and future scope.</p>
          <p class="mg-t-md"><a href="/about/project-members/" class="btn btn-secondary">Meet the advisory board <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></p>
          <div id="logo-wheel" class="uno-w-full" slot="media"><LogoWheel client:visible /></div>
        </MediaBlock>
      </Section>

      <Section>
        <MediaBlock title="About Xen Project" media="/img/flatline/data-process.svg" alt="Illustration of a laptop displaying 3D bar charts, connected to cloud storage and file management icons, symbolizing data synchronization and integration." animate>
          <p>The mission of the Xen Project is to advance virtualisation technology across a wide range of commercial and open-source domains.</p>
          <p><a href="/about/" class="btn btn-secondary">Learn about Xen Project <i class="fas fa-arrow-right"></i></a></p>
        </MediaBlock>
      </Section>
    </div>
  </article>
  <div id="cookie-banner"><CookieBanner client:idle /></div>
</BaseLayout>
